{
  "dom_id": "question-333983",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "For the initial value problem ${y}^{′}=f(x,y),y({x}_{0})={y}_{0},$ the modified Euler method can be expressed as the update formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δ{y}_{n}^{(p)} & =f({x}_{n},{y}_{n})\\cdot Δx, \\\\ {y}_{n+1} & ={y}_{n}+\\frac{1}{2}(f({x}_{n},{y}_{n})+f({x}_{n+1},{y}_{n}+Δ{y}_{n}^{(p)}))\\cdot Δx.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true when testing the stability of the modified Euler method on the test equation ${y}^{′}=-\\lambda y$ with $y=y(x),y(0)=1,x\\ge 0,\\lambda =8,$ and step size $Δx?$  \n\nI. The stability function is $R(8Δx)=1-8Δx+32(Δx)^{2}.$\n\nII. The stability region is $|32{(Δx-\\frac{1}{8})}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}|<1.$\n\nIII. The method is absolutely stable.\n\nIV. The method is stable for step size $Δx=0.6.$\n\n*Hint:* The stability function $R$ is given by ${y}_{n+1}=R(\\lambda Δx){y}_{n}.$",
  "worked_solution": "",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
